  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "opt_0": "Not at all",
      "opt_1": "Sometimes",
      "opt_2": "Very often or always",
      "info_520405": "The following pages contain statements about the effects of prescription stimulants, including Adderall®, Ritalin®, Concerta®, and Dexedrine®.",
      "used_prescription_stimulant": "Have you ever used a prescription stimulant (like Adderall® or Ritalin®) for any reason?",
      "used_prescription_stimulant_opt_1": "YES",
      "used_prescription_stimulant_opt_2": "NO",
      "instructions_520405": "Read each statement carefully and respond according to your own personal thoughts, feelings, and beliefs about prescription stimulants now. We are interested in what you think about prescription stimulants, regardless of what other people might think.\n\n\n\nWhether or not you have had actual experiences with prescription stimulants yourself, you are to answer in terms of your beliefs about prescription stimulants. It is important that you respond to every question. There are no right or wrong answers.\n\n\n\nPlease fill out the following questions according to your beliefs about the stimulant drug you know best. PLEASE BE HONEST. REMEMBER, YOUR ANSWERS ARE CONFIDENTIAL. RESPOND TO THESE ITEMS ACCORDING TO WHAT YOU PERSONALLY BELIEVE TO BE TRUE ABOUT A MODERATE AMOUNT OF STIMULANTS - HOWEVER YOU DEFINE MODERATE.",
      "distractions_disappear_stimulants": "Distractions disappear.",
      "absorb_material_first_time_stimulants": "I absorb new material the first time through.",
      "cant_focus_stimulants": "I can't focus on more than one thing at a time.",
      "focus_very_wel_stimulants": "I can focus very well.",
      "ignore_distractions_stimulants": "I can ignore distractions more easily.",
      "pay_attention_stimulants": "I can pay attention really well.",
      "study_for_hours_stimulants": "I can study for hours and hours.",
      "cant_hold_still_stimulants": "I can't hold still.",
      "cant_sleep_stimulants": "I can't sleep even if I want to.",
      "cant_calm_down_stimulants": "I can't calm down.",
      "dont_daydream_stimulants": "I don't end up daydreaming.",
      "dont_want_study_without_stimulants": "I don't want to study without it.",
      "enjoy_studying_more_stimulants": "I enjoy studying a lot more.",
      "feel_drained_next_day_stimulants": "I feel drained the next day.",
      "feel_guilty_taking_stimulants": "I feel guilty for taking it.",
      "cant_get_throughday_without_stimulants": "I feel like I can't get through the day without it.",
      "cutting_corners_stimulants": "I feel like I'm cutting corners to do well.",
      "sick_to_stomach_stimulants": "I feel sick to my stomach.",
      "feel_twitchy_stimulants": "I feel twitchy.",
      "focus_unimportant_tasks_stimulants": "I focus on unimportant tasks.",
      "annoyed_with_myself_for_stimulants": "I get annoyed with myself for taking it.",
      "get_nervous_edgy_stimulants": "I get nervous and edgy.",
      "learn_efficiently_stimulants": "I learn very efficiently.",
      "need_fewer_study_breaks_stimulants": "I need fewer breaks when I study.",
      "wish_do_well_without_stimulants": "I wish I could do as well without it.",
      "worry_im_addicted_stimulants": "I worry that I'm addicted to it.",
      "all_amped_up_stimulants": "I'm all amped up.",
      "no_trouble_sit_still_stimulants": "It's no trouble to sit still.",
      "crutch_stimulants": "I've come to see it as a crutch.",
      "ability_focus_is_better_stimulants": "My ability to focus is better.",
      "concentration_excellent_stimulants": "My concentration is excellent.",
      "focus_crystal_clear_stimulants": "My focus is crystal clear.",
      "my_head_hurts_stimulants": "My head hurts.",
      "my_memory_is_better_stimulants": "My memory is better.",
      "mind_doesnt_wander_stimulants": "My mind doesn't wander.",
      "mind_razor_sharp_stimulants": "My mind is razor sharp.",
      "thoughts_follow_more_logically_stimulants": "My thoughts follow more logically.",
      "thoughts_on_track_better_stimulants": "My thoughts stay on track better.",
      "work_more_interesting_stimulants": "My work seems more interesting.",
      "my_heart_races_stimulants": "My heart races.",
      "scoring_520405": "Scoring Procedure and Interpretation\n\n\n\nThe Prescription Stimulant Expectancy Questionnaire (PSEQ) score is calculated by averaging the item scores. Half of the items (1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 13, 23, 24, 28, 30, 31, 32, 34, 35, 36, 37, 38, and 39) are scored with 0 = \"Not at all,\" 1= \"Sometimes,\" and 2 = \"Very often or always.\" The other half of the items (3, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 25, 26, 27, 29, 33, and 40) are reverse-scored with 2 = \"Not at all,\" 1 = \"Sometimes,\" and 0 = \"Very often or always.\""
    }
  }
}